{"duration_api_ms":264765,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"[private-session]","total_cost_usd":2.6759065999999994,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40866,"cache_read_input_tokens":1569011,"output_tokens":7704,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1649},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4199,"cache_read_input_tokens":154217,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2634,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2634},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":102,"outputTokens":27515,"thinkingTokens":10001,"cacheReadInputTokens":4534513,"cacheCreationInputTokens":152287,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":152287,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.6759065999999994,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01G3926b37LfJ4ZTqdH1uQVa","tool_input":{"command":"git -C /tmp/pose-review-run-2282112913/worktree log --oneline -4; git -C /tmp/pose-review-run-2282112913/worktree diff --stat 90e6bd09..df7da2f0","description":"Show commits and diff since prior round"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":13,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Decision: approved.** Both round-1 fixes hold up, and R1-F3 is an owned low-severity follow-up. The sweep turned up no new defects.\n\nThe session again denied every Bash command (git, `go test`, `pose`). So I ran no tests or tools myself: every pass below rests on the sealed evidence plus my own reading of the code at df7da2f0.\n\n## Round-1 findings\n- **R1-F1: fixed.**\n  - **Code:** the final audit (`governance_read_view.go:388-408`) now merges the root-registry result into the primary root's audit as well as the combined one. Since `metadata()` (`:438-538`) builds freshness, limitations and the ID from those per-root audits, the result now changes them.\n  - **Change vs. budget:** a registry change or conflict is recorded as `changed`, which triggers the one retry. A final-audit budget overrun is recorded only as `unknown`, so it isn't mislabelled as a change and doesn't retry.\n  - **Tests:** `governance_read_view_d7_probe_test.go:225-375` runs review, closeout and projection through stable, once, changed, conflict and budget cases. They check freshness, approval, terminal status, coherence, coverage, limitations and that the ID changes.\n  - **Coverage:** `governanceReadViewProjectionReasonAffectsCoverage` (`obligation_projection.go:838-848`) correctly counts the registry reasons as losing coverage.\n- **R1-F2: fixed.** `governance_read_view.go:2074-2078` now shares the immutable captured bytes instead of copying them. Readers still get their own copies (`:1423`, `:1508`, `:1522`).\n- **R1-F3: not fixed, but tracked.** The substring match is still at `index_generation_build.go:205`. The spec records it as an open follow-up (`.pose/specs/…:409`, owner `@pose-maintainers`, low, review by 2026-12-06). I accept that as a tracked risk.\n\n## Sweep\nI re-read these files, focusing on the parts that changed since round 1:\n- the final audit, `metadata()` and the per-root audit (`governance_read_view.go`)\n- caller isolation in `readFile` and `open`\n- the projection's retry and coverage handling\n- review and closeout's use of the read view\n- the index-build capture and its retry\n- the write guard and scoped guard\n- the action write scope (`action_write_scope.go:1-120`)\n- the newly listed `.pose/policy/delegation.json` and its scaffold exclusion (`distpolicy.go:115-118`)\n\n`delegation.json` holds no secrets or key material. No new defects found.\n\n## Structural facts\n- **SD-0cf58a00** (`validation-matrix.json`): caused by R10 and Validation V7. It adds the required race check `governance-read-view-integration` and the explicit `-count=1` checks.\n- **SD-5c5ba300** (the ADR): caused by the spec constraint that the B34 ADR must be accepted before the contract changes. It is the basis for D2–D9.\n- **SD-98ca1442** (`delegation.json`): caused by D8. This is instance-only delegation configuration for the independent review task, and it's excluded from the scaffold (`distpolicy.go:118`). The narrower session regex answers the retained capture failure `rrn-db41024e48aa50af`; it touches no engine contract.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/index_generation_build.go\", \"line\": 205, \"summary\": \"Index build failure code 'federated-roadmap' is still selected by substring match on error text instead of a typed/sentinel error; recorded as an owned open follow-up in the spec.\", \"action\": \"Replace the substring classification with a typed error while preserving the code, receipts and negative controls.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-06\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go:388-408 merges the registry audit into perRoot[op.primary] consumed by metadata (:438-538); regressions pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_d7_probe_test.go:225-375 cover review/closeout/projection with stable/once/changed/conflict/budget; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration pass\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F2\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go:2074-2078 shares immutable captured bytes after close/join; caller isolation kept at :1423, :1508, :1522\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/index_generation_build.go:205 unchanged; accepted as owned follow-up in .pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:409 (owner @pose-maintainers, review 2026-12-06)\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Re-read the operation final audit, metadata and per-root audit, readFile/open caller isolation, obligation projection retry/coverage and the reason classifier, review/closeout read-view application and retry, index build capture/retry (governance_read_view_capture.go, index_generation_build.go), write guard and scoped guard, action write scope, the new registry regressions, the delegation.json change and its distpolicy exclusion. Bash (git/go test/pose) was denied in this session, so mechanical judgments rely on sealed evidence plus source reading.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:409\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:POSE.md:372\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cross-component-integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-profile-parity-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go:388\"},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:POSE.md:372\"},\n    {\"id\": \"milestone-exit-gate-pose-state-consistency-and-recovery-governance-read-view\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_d7_probe_test.go:225\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:pose-mcp/internal/cli/index_generation_build.go:39\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:.pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/distpolicy/distpolicy.go:118\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"file:pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go:2075\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Command execution denied in this review session; no sealed evidence ID for this tool.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a47e